abstract: >-
  OpenGenesis-BioCore is a local-first, extensible bioinformatics platform
  designed for reproducible analysis workflows on Windows and Linux. Version
  0.6.0 builds on the canonical small-variant, Workflow Engine 2.0, and Project
  & Sample Workspace layers with project-scoped cohort/group registries,
  deterministic verified-artifact selection, compatibility and QC gates,
  frozen cohort analysis snapshots, canonical multi-sample matrix and
  case/control association reuse, durable execution/recovery lineage,
  verified result manifests, result browsing and multi-format reporting.
  The release retains the C++20 native core, localhost-only browser interface,
  SQLite persistence, native plugins, exact-version workflow templates,
  scientific benchmark gates, and local-first provenance model.

